  "result": "`python3 -m shop quote a:12.5:2` now prints 27.06, and all 11 tests pass.\n\n**Root cause:** `to_cents` in `shop/money.py` padded the fraction on the wrong side. `\"5\".rjust(2, \"0\")` gives `\"05\"`, so `12.5` was parsed as 12.05 (1205 cents) instead of 12.50 (1250 cents). Every one-decimal price was undercharged. The quote was 2 \u00d7 12.05 = 24.10, plus 8.25% tax on that, which came to 26.09.\n\n**Fix:** changed `rjust` to `ljust` in `shop/money.py:9`. I also dropped the `or 0`, which was redundant since `int(\"00\")` already gives 0.\n\n**Test:** `pytest` isn't installed here, so I ran the suite with `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -t .`. I added `tests/test_money.py` to cover one-decimal, two-decimal, no-decimal, too-many-decimals, and `fmt` round-trip cases. I removed the `__pycache__` directories the test runs created.\n\nI did not commit anything.",
